extends RefCounted
class_name HPProtocol

## Authoritative protocol shared by the world server and every client.
## OWNER: server repository. The client copy is generated by `dev.ps1 sync-sim`;
## never edit `client/addons/hpmmo_sim/` by hand.
##
## This file is the source of the contract document `contracts/protocol.md`
## (generated by `client/tools/workspace/extract_protocol.py`).

## Bumped whenever a message shape, semantics, or rule constant changes in a way
## that makes older clients disagree. Clients whose version differs are refused
## at join instead of silently desyncing.
## v5: per-map state and the server-authorized map-transfer exchange.
## v6: encounter lifecycle - mob AI state in the snapshot state byte and the
##     boss telegraph message (server-owned release tick, client-rendered
##     warning) from the creature pass.
## v7: the session is bound to the character it plays - a character-bound
##     session is validated and bound at join, and a `sim_bind_character`
##     exchange lets a session that joined without one name the character it
##     wants (the server proves ownership before binding). A v6 client would
##     join unbound and never save, so the mismatch is refused like any other.
## v9: chat channels - `sim_chat_line(channel, uid, name, house, text)` carries
##     a routed player line ("local" to players within CHAT_LOCAL_RADIUS on the
##     speaker's map, "shout" - a line starting with "!" - to everyone); the
##     plain `sim_chat_event` stays for system text only.
## v10: server-authoritative quests - `sim_talk_request(npc_name)` asks the
##     authority to count a conversation (range-checked against the NPC), and
##     the stats payload carries `quest_active` / `quest_progress` plus the
##     house standing fields. Kill, monolith, refine and visit progress is
##     observed by the server; a v9 client would never progress, so it is
##     refused like any other mismatch.
## v11: item instances - a non-stackable item (wand, robe, broom, accessory) is
##     its own bag entry with a `uid` and `bonuses`, and `sim_equipment_request`
##     gains a trailing `uid` naming the instance to equip. A v10 client would
##     call the old six-argument RPC, so the mismatch is refused at join.
## v12: critical hits and the combo chain - `sim_damage_event` gains a trailing
##     `flags` (HIT_* bits) so every client can draw the crit / finisher number
##     the server rolled.
## v13: skill training - `sim_skill_request(spell_id)` asks the authority to
##     spend one skill point on a spell, and the stats payload carries `skills`
##     ({spell_id: level}) and `skill_points`. Damage, cooldown and effect
##     duration scale with the caster's skill level, so a v12 client would
##     predict the wrong cooldowns; the mismatch is refused at join.
## v14: creature catalog - `sim_mob_info(uid, info)` (reliable) tells a client a
##     mob's display name, level and elite flag the first time it enters the
##     interest set and again whenever the mob's meta revision changes (respawn
##     re-rolls elite). Snapshots stay 30 bytes; a v13 client would label every
##     mob with its scene defaults. Mob variants 4-6 (forest troll, mountain
##     troll, dementor) are part of v14: a v13 client cannot render them.
##     `sim_world_event(kind, data)` announces world bosses realm-wide.
##     Parties: `/commands` ride the chat intent; `sim_party_state(state)` and
##     `sim_party_invite(from_name)` answer the members.
##     Instanced maps travel as `<base>#<slot>` map ids; `sim_dungeon_state`
##     carries a copy's run state (step, open gates, message).
## v15: the Forbidden Corridor - mob variants 7-13 (pixie, armours, Devil's
##     Snare and its vines, Fluffy and its heads); mob info carries
##     `parts_down`; `sim_push(force)` (reliable) gives the owning client the
##     impulse the authority shoved its body with; loot may carry an owner
##     (personal dungeon loot: sent to and taken by that player only); the
##     stats payload carries `titles`.
## v16: loot drops as one chest per kill. `sim_loot_event` carries the chest's
##     slot list (re-sent when a partial take changes it), and
##     `sim_pickup_request(uid, slot)` takes one slot (-1 = all that fits).
## v17: quest log, learned skills and status points. Several quests are open
##     at once; the stats payload carries `quests` ({progress: {id: n}, ready:
##     [ids], done: [ids]}) instead of `quest_active` / `quest_progress`, and a
##     finished quest pays only when `sim_quest_claim(quest_id)` claims it. A
##     skill at level 0 is not learned (casts are refused `skill_locked`); the
##     payload's `skill_points` count the starter pick. `sim_attribute_request
##     (stat)` spends a status point; the payload carries `attributes` and
##     `attribute_points`.
## v18: death is a choice. `sim_respawn_request(mode)` picks RESPAWN_HERE (where
##     the body fell, part health) or RESPAWN_TOWN (the map's respawn point);
##     both unlock `respawn_ready_tick` (in the stats payload) and the body
##     returns to town on its own at `respawn_tick`. `sim_player_info(uid,
##     info)` carries another player's name, house and level on first sight
##     and on every change (players used to show the default name).
## v19: the Blackweb Caverns - mob variants 14-15 (Venomfang, Broodguard) and
##     16, the Webbound Seal Stone (a monolith's variant names its body; 0/1 is
##     the Dark Monolith); the stats payload carries `webbed_until_tick` and
##     the burn clock with its `burn_kind` (spider venom rides it).
## v20: the Floo Network (data/travel.json). `sim_travel_request(node_id,
##     dest_id)`: standing at a fireplace, an empty dest only learns it; a dest
##     spends Floo Powder and runs the ordinary transfer (grant -> ready ->
##     commit, spawn id `floo:<dest>`, same map allowed). The stats payload
##     carries `floo_known` (the fireplaces this character can travel to).
## v21: Portkeys. `sim_portkey_place(dest_id)` sets the owner's boot down
##     (travel.json `portkey`), `sim_portkey_grab(id, hold)` holds on / lets go,
##     and `sim_portkey_state(state)` tells the owner and the owner's party what
##     the boot is doing (phase placed / fired / gone, holders, fire tick).
##     A fired Portkey grants each holder an ordinary transfer (spawn id
##     `portkey:<dest>`).
## v22: lean stats. `sim_stats_event` carries the full sheet (bag, gear,
##     quests, skills) only to the body's owner and only when it changed; a
##     fight or regeneration sends the vitals alone, and other players get the
##     public part (uid, hp, max_hp, level, dead, mounted) when it changes.
##     Another player's worn gear (slot -> {id, tier}) rides `sim_player_info`
##     as `gear`. A v21 client would draw every other player bare-handed.
## v23: mob variants 17-19 (Inferius Lake Warden, Goblin Teller, Goblin Vault
##     Guard). A v22 client would draw them as the variant-1 Inferius.
## v24: mob variant 20 (Goblin Hexer, the wandless caster of the mixed goblin
##     packs). A v23 client would draw it as the variant-1 Inferius.
## v25: snapshots carry a status byte (STATUS_* crowd control and damage over
##     time on the body: stun, freeze, slow, bleed, burn, poison, knocked,
##     disarmed), 31 bytes per entity, so every client draws the same effects.
## v26: GA (game admin) - `ga` in player info and the owner's stats (the
##     emblem over the name), `/ga` chat commands, and the world's weather
##     (`sim_weather` {rain}) sent on change and on joining.
const PROTOCOL_VERSION := 26

## Death choice (v18 `sim_respawn_request`).
const RESPAWN_TOWN := 0
const RESPAWN_HERE := 1

## Per-hit presentation bits carried by `sim_damage_event` / `entity_hit`.
const HIT_CRIT := 1
const HIT_FINISHER := 2
const HIT_PIERCE := 4
## Crowd-control efsun procs that landed with the hit (stun, slow, ignite).
const HIT_STUN := 8
const HIT_SLOW := 16
const HIT_BURN := 32

## Simulation / replication rates.
const SIM_HZ := 20
const SIM_DT := 1.0 / 20.0
const SNAPSHOT_HZ := 10
const SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL_TICKS := SIM_HZ / SNAPSHOT_HZ

## How long a client's movement input stays valid while packets are missing.
## Input older than this is discarded (the player simply stops accelerating).
## Inputs travel at 20 Hz unreliably, so this rides out a few lost frames; a
## client that froze or lost its connection stops instead of running on.
const INPUT_BUFFER_MS := 300
## A cast request arriving this close to the end of recovery is queued instead
## of refused (bounded input buffer, 100-150 ms).
const CAST_QUEUE_MS := 120
## Damage within this window of a kill credits the player with the reward.
const KILL_CREDIT_MS := 10000

## ENet channels. Keeping movement off the reliable channel is what stops a lost
## packet from stalling the player in place.
const CH_SNAPSHOT := 0
const CH_EVENT := 1
const CH_INTENT := 2
const CH_INPUT := 3

## Interest filtering.
const INTEREST_RADIUS := 70.0
const MAX_ENTITIES_PER_SNAPSHOT := 30
const DEFAULT_MAP := "grounds"

## Map transfer. A client that requested a transfer but never
## acknowledged readiness must not strand its character between maps, so the
## reservation expires and the character returns to its last valid safe spawn.
## Test affordance: HPMMO_DEV_TRANSFER_TIMEOUT_MS (never set in production).
const TRANSFER_TIMEOUT_MS := 15000

static func transfer_timeout_ms() -> int:
	var raw := OS.get_environment("HPMMO_DEV_TRANSFER_TIMEOUT_MS")
	if raw != "" and raw.is_valid_int():
		return maxi(250, int(raw))
	return TRANSFER_TIMEOUT_MS

